<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Penoles outlines mining output.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Penoles outlines mining output.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrias Penoles, the world's largest refined silver producer, detailed on Tuesday metal content volumes produced by the company's mining division in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Precious metals in kg, base metals in tonnes.</p>
<p>    Metal	   Q197	   Q196	  Q496</p>
<p>    Gold	    1,237	  1,027	  1,248</p>
<p>    Silver	272,299	234,157	278,477</p>
<p>    Lead	   16,699	 17,437	 18,029</p>
<p>    Zinc	   31,469	 29,032	 32,986</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
<p>E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
